@*
    A password box whose typed text can be checked before it is saved: an API key pasted into the
    Solcast or OpenWeatherMap field, a broker password, a new sign-in password. Secret (the stored value
    behind Reveal) only shows what is already saved; this shows what is in the box now.

    The toggle is a plain script (js/reveal.js) rather than a Blazor event, because the sign-in, setup
    and reset pages are static server rendering with no circuit to call back into, and one mechanism
    serves both. Blazor never renders the box's type differently, so a re-render leaves a revealed box
    revealed; the button's state lives in aria-pressed, which only the script writes.
*@
<span class="reveal">
    @ChildContent
    @if (!Disabled)
    {
        <button type="button" class="reveal-toggle">
            <span class="reveal-show">@SharedText.Reveal</span>
            <span class="reveal-hide">@SharedText.Hide</span>
        </button>
    }
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The password input itself.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// No toggle, for a box nobody may type into (a form without a login): there is nothing to check,
    /// and a read-only page offers no buttons at all.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }
}
